IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- LAYER 1, MODULE 6: REGULATION 3 (saving).
--
-- Regulation 3 preserves, for a person who would have got more under the revoked 1976
-- Regulations by virtue of their transitional provisions and savings, the greater
-- amount. The amount that the 1976 Regulations (with regulations 3 and 4 of the 1998
-- Amendment Regulations) would have given is OUT OF TEXT: none of those instruments
-- is an input. It is therefore a `MAYBE NUMBER` taken as a plain input:
--   * NOTHING means that no transitional provision or saving would have applied to
--     this person, so that the amount these Regulations prescribe stands;
--   * JUST x means that one would, and x is the weekly amount it would have given.
-- Neither is ever replaced by 0, which would be a plausible default and not the text.

§ `Regulation 3: saving`

§§ `Regulation 3(2): which transitional provisions and savings`

-- src:56 | (2) In paragraph (1) “the relevant transitional provisions and savings” means—
-- src:57 | (a) in the case of child benefit payable under SSCBA, regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations 1998 ; and
-- src:58 | (b) in the case of child benefit payable under SSCB(NI)A, regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1998 .
@ref reg 3(2) (src:56-58)
GIVEN act IS AN `Act under which child benefit is payable`
GIVETH A `Transitional provisions and savings in regulation 3(2)`
`the relevant transitional provisions and savings for` act MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `child benefit payable under SSCBA` THEN `regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations 1998`    -- (a)
    WHEN `child benefit payable under SSCB(NI)A` THEN `regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1998`    -- (b)

§§ `Regulation 3(1): the greater amount shall be payable`

-- The two instruments the paragraph speaks of, in the text's own words and without
-- the leading "the"; the tests show that they are rows 1 and 2 of the Table in
-- regulation 4, revoked in whole.
-- src:52 | (1) Despite the revocation, by regulation 4 of these Regulations, of—
-- src:53 | (a) the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) Regulations 1976 , and
-- src:54 | (b) the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1976 ,
@ref reg 3(1) (src:52-54)
`the earlier Regulations named in regulation 3(1)` MEANS
    LIST "Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) Regulations 1976"
       , "Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1976"

-- src:55 | if the amount of child benefit which would have been payable under those Regulations would, by virtue of the relevant transitional provisions and savings (had they remained in force), be greater than the amount prescribed by these Regulations, the greater amount shall be payable.
@ref reg 3(1) (src:55)
GIVEN prescribed IS A NUMBER
      saved IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` prescribed saved MEANS
    CONSIDER saved
    WHEN NOTHING THEN prescribed
    WHEN JUST earlier THEN IF earlier GREATER THAN prescribed THEN earlier ELSE prescribed

-- The same, applied to a weekly rate that may itself be not covered: NOTHING stays
-- NOTHING, because "the amount prescribed by these Regulations" is then not known.
-- src:55 | if the amount of child benefit which would have been payable under those Regulations would, by virtue of the relevant transitional provisions and savings (had they remained in force), be greater than the amount prescribed by these Regulations, the greater amount shall be payable.
@ref reg 3(1) (src:55)
GIVEN `the amount prescribed by regulation 2` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      saved IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly amount payable after the saving in regulation 3` `the amount prescribed by regulation 2` saved MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount prescribed by regulation 2`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST (`the greater amount payable under regulation 3(1)` prescribed saved)
